:: jessie [c4 trainer]
<p>There is a Mergimal Trainer standing near the base of the cliff, playing with a fidget spinner. They yawn and roll their eyes as you approach.</p>
<<say 'Jessie' 'images/characters/portrait_0.webp'>>I suppose you want to have a contest?<</say>>
<ul class='choices'>
  <li>[[Absolutely!->jessie: start]]</li>
  <li>[[Ask them what's new.->404]]</li>
  <li>[[Maybe another time: continue exploring.->c4]]</li>
</ul>

:: jessie: start [c4 trainer contest]
<<say 'Jessie' 'images/characters/portrait_0.webp'>>I was afraid you'd say that.<br />
Listen, there's not a ton to do around here, but there are a ton of rocks.<br />
Big ones, little ones, heavy metal or punk ones...get it? Because they're types of rock.<</say>>
<ul class='choices'>
  <li><<link 'Oh...yeah, that\'s hilarious.' 'jessie: start 2'>><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: jessie: start 2
<p>Jessie yawns again.</p>
<<say 'Jessie' 'images/characters/portrait_0.webp'>>Yeah, yeah.... Not the best joke. I told you, I'm bored, okay?<</say>>
<p>Jessie shakes themself awake and puts the fidget spinner in their pocket.</p>
<<say 'Jessie' 'images/characters/portrait_0.webp'>>Well, you're going to stack some rocks. It's called nature art.<br />
If your art is artsy enough to make me feel it in my heart, you win.<br />
I can't join you in lifting any rocks because I'm far too artsy for that kind of labor.<</say>>
<ul class='choices'>
  <li><<link 'Get started.' 'jessie: start 3'>><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: jessie: start 3
<<say 'Jessie' 'images/characters/portrait_0.webp'>>How many rocks are you putting in your stack?<</say>>
<p><<numberbox '$rocksPerPile' 0 autofocus>></p>
<ul class='choices'>
  <li><<link 'Tell them how many rocks in each pile.' 'jessie: stacking'>><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: jessie: stacking [c4 trainer contest]
<<if $rocksPerPile > 20>>
	<<set $rocksPerPile = 14>>
    <<say 'Jessie' 'images/characters/portrait_0.webp'>>Whoa, it's about to fall! You better stop right there...<br />
    You're at $rocksPerPile now. Good.<</say>>
<<elseif $rocksPerPile < 4>>
	<<set $rocksPerPile = 6>>
	<<say 'Jessie' 'images/characters/portrait_0.webp'>>Hey, you should really keep going. You need more rocks for it to be real art.<br />
  A bit more...<br />
  Yeah, $rocksPerPile rocks should do the trick.<</say>>
<<else>>
	<<say 'Jessie' 'images/characters/portrait_0.webp'>>Hey, that's a nice stack! Now there are... $rocksPerPile rocks on the pile, right?<</say>>
<</if>>
<p>Jessie blinks their eyes slowly and holds back a yawn.</p>
<<say 'Jessie' 'images/characters/portrait_0.webp'>>Now make some more piles with $rocksPerPile rocks in each one.<br />
Remember to make it really artsy looking, or I might fall asleep on you.<</say>>
<p><<numberbox '$rockPiles' 0 autofocus>></p>
<ul class='choices'>
  <li><<link 'Tell them how many piles.' 'jessie: answer'>><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: jessie: answer [c4 trainer contest]
<<if $rockPiles > 20>>
  <p>You ran out of rocks after 19 piles...</p>
    <<set $rockPiles to 19>>
<</if>>
<<say 'Jessie' 'images/characters/portrait_0.webp'>>Nice work! You made $rockPiles piles with $rocksPerPile in each one.<br />
How did you even have the energy to do that? That's a lot of rocks!<</say>>
<p>The trainer scratches their head and looks slightly confused.</p>
<<say 'Jessie' 'images/characters/portrait_0.webp'>>Umm, help me out...<br />
How many rocks did you use in total?<</say>>
<p><<numberbox '$totalRocks' 0 autofocus>></p>
<ul class='choices'>
  <li><<link 'Tell them how many total rocks.' 'jessie: end'>><</link>></li>
</ul>

:: jessie: end [c4 trainer contest]
<<if $totalRocks == $rocksPerPile * $rockPiles>>
  <<say 'Jessie' 'images/characters/portrait_0.webp'>>That's right! Nice work. Here, take this fidget spinner. I have a few of them and they're great for when you're really bored, like I am.<</say>>
  <<writeentry 'I got a fidget spinner from Jessie for stacking rocks.'>>
  <ul class='choices'>
    <li><<link 'Say thanks and continue exploring.' $players[$activePlayer].characters[$activeCharacter].worldMapPosition>><</link>></li>
  </ul>
<<else>>
    <<say 'Jessie' 'images/characters/portrait_0.webp'>>Hmm...not quite. Do you want to try again? We're mupliplying $rocksPerPile by $rockPiles.<</say>>
    <<numberbox '$totalRocks' 0 autofocus>>
    <ul class='choices'>
      <li><<link 'Try again.' 'jessie: end'>><</link>></li>
      <li><<link 'Give up for now. Keep exploring Route 002.' $players[$activePlayer].characters[$activeCharacter].worldMapPosition>><</link>></li>
    </ul>
<</if>>